- op: discuss  # b88b
  at: '2026-09-24T07:21:41Z'  # b88b
  by: agent  # b88b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b88b
  clock: 4  # b88b
  nonce: b88b  # b88b
  message: "DONE in PR #1174. The proposal was built as written: a session-start reader, cached, silent on outage, suppressed by an open row.\n\nMECHANISM: .agent/hooks/_shared/cron_status_nudge.py, called as _append_cron_status from every mode branch of session_start_logic.sh. All four vendors' session-start hooks source that file.\n- It runs `ci-debug cron-status`, lists each red workflow's failing STEPS, and walks back one cron verdict at a time to the commit where the step FIRST went red.\n- It stays silent when green or pending, when the CI host is unreachable, when output can't be parsed, and under CI or HG_SKIP_CRON_NUDGE.\n- It suppresses a step that an OPEN row names at a red commit.\n- The network half is cached for 1h.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, live on dev b0dcfd1e41 (the cron is red at d31439e6 until the 13:00 UTC firing):\n  python3 .agent/hooks/_shared/cron_status_nudge.py .   -> rc 0, 17.4 s cold, 1.2 s cached\n  \"The cron CI is RED and no open tracker row names it: full-suite (`test-all-packages`) red at d31439e6, 7 commit(s) back, first red at d31439e6. Read `./scripts/ci-debug cron-status`, then fix it or file a row naming the step and commit.\"\n`test-agent-infra` was correctly suppressed, because WI-juzoz names that step at d31439e6. Sourcing session_start_logic.sh in OFF mode shows the line as an \"ALSO (separate item)\".\n\nNOT ASSERTED:\n- That a SessionStart hook runs with its full ~17 s cold budget under every vendor's hook timeout. Not measured per vendor. The cache makes the cold path at most hourly.\n- The per-PR detection latency, which is unchanged by design (owner decision 08-30)."  # b88b
